  "summary": {
    "plain": "The NIST beam experiment re-measured how well its neutron counter works, five times more precisely than before, and so updated its 2005 neutron lifetime to 887.7 seconds with an uncertainty of about 2.2 seconds.",
    "technical": "Direct calibration of the 6Li neutron monitor against a totally absorbing detector to 0.057% (five-fold improvement), without nuclear-data cross sections; the 2005 result 886.3 ± 1.2 stat ± 3.2 syst s becomes tau_n = 887.7 ± 1.2 stat ± 1.9 syst s."
  },
  "title": "Improved Determination of the Neutron Lifetime",
